{"type":"message","id":"6f481947","parentId":"1bed4c6b","timestamp":"2026-05-18T03:39:04.017Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The GET requests work with `X-API-KEY` header but not the POST /send endpoint. Let me try to use `Authorization` header for GET to see if that also fails, then understand the auth pattern better.\n\nActually, from the GET responses we can see:\n- GET /history works with `X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key`\n- POST /send returns 1101 with `X-API-KEY` but 401 Unauthorized with `Authorization: Bearer`\n\nSo the /send endpoint might have a different implementation that has a bug. Let me try a different approach - maybe use a different base URL path, or maybe the POST body needs a different field name.\n\n\nWait, error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers is a `worker_exception` in the Worker itself - that's a server-side issue, not an auth problem. The Worker code is throwing an unhandled exception when it receives that POST request. Let me test the GET endpoint with an `Authorization: Bearer` header to see if it works there too, or try sending a basic test message to see what's actually happening. But I'm also noticing the timestamp on the last arbitration message shows 23:50, and that's only a couple hours before the current time - let me just focus on what's most relevant here.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-4c8f03b6-b5dc-432e-ab5f-2777493d43bd","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -v -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"heartbeat test 03:30\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-bcb04338-d2b4-4655-9caa-17203c298588","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" 2>&1 | head -5"}}],"a